Package: pve-disk-io
Version: 1.0.0
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Depends: perl, libjson-perl, librrds-perl, systemd
Recommends: pve-manager
Maintainer: grioghar <noreply@users.noreply.github.com>
Homepage: https://github.com/grioghar/proxmox-disk-io
Description: Disk I/O panel for Proxmox VE
 Adds a live view of what a node's physical disks are doing and which guests
 are responsible, plus recorded history on the node and per-guest Summary
 pages.
 .
 I/O that reaches a disk through a FUSE pool such as mergerfs is credited to
 the container or host process that asked for it, rather than to the pool's
 daemon, which is what the block layer sees.
